5.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: The description is the familiar stroke-pattern riddle for 晶 jīng.

晶 is three 日 put side by side.  If you read the three 日’s off from left to right you get

* 一横一横再一横 – the three top horizontals, one for each 日;
* 一竖一竖再一竖 – the three left-hand verticals, one for each 日;
* 一竖在左一竖在右 – the left and right uprights of the middle 日, i.e. the
  framing 竖 of a single 日;
* 一竖一竖再一竖 – the three right-hand verticals, one for each 日.

Together the three 日 give the 12-stroke character 晶, literally “three suns”, the
common writing for ‘bright, crystal, clear’. It is the classic “three 日” 晶
that is usually quoted in this horizontal/vertical stroke riddle.

